Dear John,

OK, I misinterpreted you then (or didn't read well enough....).

Yes, then you can estimate things, but you just can't compare your estimates with a directly observable quantity. Except perhaps if you count observed extinction and colonization events over the two-year intervals and then combine your estimates from the model over the same interval. That sounds a little messy to me and would probably be much easier using MCMC in a Bayesian analysis, because of the ease with which derived quantities = functions of params can be obtained there.

Best regards  ---- Marc

