Just thinking on the screen here, and could well be completely misguided, but it seems to me that lacking any observations that would directly inform first order Markov-processes could complicate things regardless of how the model is fit.  There might be some multi-modality in the likelihood surface associated with difficulty distinguishing between a lot of turnover or limited turnover--something like a hidden covariance between gamma and eps. If so, seems like there might be a lot of estimate sensitivity to model structure (e.g., covariates having 'significant'  and similar directional influence on both dynamic parameters, but very little influence when modeled as influencing only one dynamic parameter). No idea whether this falls under the header of tricky or problematic (and of course, I certainly may be completely wrong about all of this, period).

